o 5:00 p.m. at the Division of the State Architect located at 1102 Q Street, Third Floor Conference Rooms A/B, Sacramento, California, 95811. A meeting notice and agenda of the meeting is available for download.\n\n  * 12/07/06 SHBSB Agenda and Meeting Notice (PDF - 32 KB)\n  * 12/07/06 SHBSB Minutes (PDF - 50 KB)  \n\n##### SHBSB Meeting Dates and Activities for 2005\n\n##### November 29, 2005\n\nThe SHBSB considered the adoption of revised language for Chapter 10, and for a new Appendix Chapter for the 2006 California Historical Building Code.\n\n  * Chapter 10 (PDF - 16 KB)\n  * Appendix A (PDF - 40 KB)\n\n##### October 13, 2005\n\nThe SHBSB held a meeting regarding amendments to the California Historical Building Code on Thursday, October 13, 2005. The meeting will be held at the Division of the State Architect, Conference Room B, Suite 5100, 1102 Q Street, Sacramento, California. An agenda and meeting notice is available for download in PDF format.\n\n  * 10/13/05 SHBSB Agenda and Meeting Notice (PDF - 33 KB)\n  * Board Approved Express Terms and Initial Statements of Reasons will be posted when revised (10/17/05).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMicrosoft Word - IEMP_Guideline_Master_Summer2026 (https://www.ges.kyoto-u.ac.jp/ges/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/IEMP_Guideline_Master_Summer2026.pdf)\nciteturn1110search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Date & Time August 25 - 27, 2026 9:00 -18:00 (JST) each day * The date and time of the interview for each applicant will be specified from the above period.(Applicants cannot specify the interview date or time) * The interview session is approximately 35 minutes long.\nTesting Service) will not be accepted. The score records of TOEFL-CBT, TOEFL-ITP, TOEIC Bridge, \nTOEIC-IP and IELTS (General Training Module) are not acceptable. \n \nNote: Applicants may find the following information useful, if they have several test scores and \nwish to identify the most